# Keep the Rust image build context small + keep docs out of layers.
#
# PUBLIC variant, shipped by build-public-export.sh step 3 (like gitignore.public).
# It drops a block of exclusions for paths that do not exist in this repository —
# they excluded nothing here, and enumerating them served no build purpose. The
# blanket `*.md` below already covers every Markdown file regardless of name.
.git/
**/target/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
**/__pycache__/
.env
.env.*
# TLS material — never in an image layer (no Rust build embeds certs). The
# gateway/ingest build context is the repo root, so exclude these explicitly.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
# Docs must never enter an image layer.
*.md
# Not needed to build the Rust binaries (gateway/ingest + their workspace members).
apps/
# ...EXCEPT the authoritative Drizzle migrations: the gateway embeds them at
# compile time via db::apply_migrations include_str!("../../../../apps/web/db/
# migrations/*.sql"). Re-include just that dir; the rest of the Next.js app stays out.
!apps/web/db/migrations
!apps/web/db/migrations/**
evals/
ml/
bench/
docs/
runbooks/
spec/
packages/sdk-python/
packages/sdk-typescript/
packages/cli/
